      "writtenOn": "2026-04-14T17:03:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LoadCrossRefStream() (line 936) uses break, and RebuildCrossRef() (lines 815, 824) uses an inverted condition (if (obj_num \u003c\u003d kMaxObjectNumber)). Both silently skip entries that exceed the limit without triggering a rebuild. This CL keeps continue to stay consistent with those existing patterns.\n\nIf the preferred direction is to unify all three paths to return false and trigger a rebuild, I\u0027m happy to do that as a follow-up refactoring CL that updates all three sites together. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "734f0fda_cb560576",
